{
  "version": 1,
  "about": "What backend/tracking/topics.py reads a task's name against. Every skill-tree node (data/skill_nodes.json) is already a topic under its tree; this file adds what a node name alone can't catch: finer topics under a node (recursive counting under Counting), more ways people write a topic (dp, bfs, u-sub), the extra subsubjects a tree doesn't cover (real analysis), which trees count as part of each subject, and the contests, exams, courses and sites a task or goal can name, each with the topics it tests in the order it tests them most. A topic that is not a node of its own can name the node its tasks count toward with `node` (an id, or tree to id), which is how finished tasks move a tile on the skill tree (backend/tracking/skill_progress.py).",
